DREAM macOS port: faad2 2.11.4 DRM fix - HCR last-segment merge with more than 32 leftover bits.

When the HCR area is longer than the sum of the segment widths, the remaining bits
extend the last segment. hcr.c merges them with what is left of that segment after
its priority codeword. For a leftover of 33..63 bits it took showbits_hcr(.., 32), the
TOP 32 bits of the leftover, as its low word; the correct low word is the leftover's
bufa. Such frames decoded to garbage (often reported as error 17). Found by Barclay
(libxaac DRM encoder, which avoids the layout); fdk-aac decodes these streams.

diff --git a/libfaad/hcr.c b/libfaad/hcr.c
index 91c294f..7b6a4de 100644
--- a/libfaad/hcr.c
+++ b/libfaad/hcr.c
@@ -338,10 +338,14 @@ uint8_t reordered_spectral_data(NeAACDecStruct *hDecoder, ic_stream *ics,
 
                                                 if (segment[numberOfSegments-1].len > 32)
                                                 {
+                                                    /* leftover of the last segment (len 33..63 bits) goes into the
+                                                       low len bits: high part = bufb (masked), low part = the whole
+                                                       bufa. showbits_hcr(.., 32) returned the TOP 32 bits instead,
+                                                       i.e. the wrong bits (DREAM macOS port patch) */
                                                     segment[numberOfSegments-1].bufb = segment[numberOfSegments].bufb +
                                                         showbits_hcr(&segment[numberOfSegments-1], segment[numberOfSegments-1].len - 32);
                                                     segment[numberOfSegments-1].bufa = segment[numberOfSegments].bufa +
-                                                        showbits_hcr(&segment[numberOfSegments-1], 32);
+                                                        segment[numberOfSegments-1].bufa;
                                                 } else {
                                                     segment[numberOfSegments-1].bufa = segment[numberOfSegments].bufa +
                                                         showbits_hcr(&segment[numberOfSegments-1], segment[numberOfSegments-1].len);
